debark: base: "not-a-base" is neither a builtin base id nor a file that exists
builtin bases: debian:12/desktop, debian:12/minimal, debian:12/server, debian:13/desktop, debian:13/minimal, debian:13/server, ubuntu:22.04/desktop, ubuntu:22.04/minimal, ubuntu:22.04/server, ubuntu:24.04/desktop, ubuntu:24.04/minimal, ubuntu:24.04/server, ubuntu:26.04/desktop, ubuntu:26.04/minimal, ubuntu:26.04/server
or pass a path to a base definition file (see docs/formats.md)

Usage:
  debark snapshot from-base BASE [flags]

Flags:
      --arch string      dpkg architecture to describe (default: this machine's)
      --backend string   auto, local or container (default: config backend, else auto)
  -h, --help             help for from-base
      --image string     override the container image for the container backend
      --interactive      ask for anything not given on the command line (a terminal is required)
      --out string       output path for the snapshot archive (default: derived from the base id and architecture)

Global Flags:
      --config string        config file path (overrides XDG discovery)
      --json                 print the documented JSON object for this command instead of human text
      --json-events string   stream NDJSON evidence events to PATH, or "-" for stdout
      --no-color             disable coloured output (also honours NO_COLOR and TERM=dumb)
      --profile string       named config profile to apply
